  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "sc_pkcs15_decode_pukdf_entry",
    "file": "opensc/src/libopensc/pkcs15-pubkey.c",
    "description": "Double-free due to ownership confusion of obj->content (der). In sc_pkcs15_decode_pukdf_entry, ASN.1 decode stores allocated direct-value bytes into obj->content.value/len via der. On error path (r < 0), the function explicitly frees der->value (line ~355) but does not null/reset obj->content. Caller/harness then calls sc_pkcs15_free_object(), which calls sc_pkcs15_free_object_content() and frees obj->content.value again, triggering double-free. Crash happens in sc_pkcs15_free_object_content, but root cause is premature manual free in decode_pukdf_entry without clearing state.",
    "conditions": "Trigger requires sc_pkcs15_decode_pukdf_entry to allocate obj->content.value during ASN.1 decode and then return an error after that allocation (e.g., malformed PKCS#15 public key entry causing later decode/validation failure). Data flow: fuzz harness allocates obj, calls decode_entries[i](..., obj, ...); when decode returns non-success, harness still calls sc_pkcs15_free_object(obj). Because decode_pukdf_entry already freed der->value on its error path and left obj->content fields intact, final object cleanup frees same pointer again."
  },
